<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <meta name="referrer" content="no-referrer">
  <meta http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy" content="default-src 'none'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self'; connect-src 'self'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; object-src 'none'">
  <title>Foundry · Operator</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="operator.css">
  <script src="operator.js" defer></script>
</head>
<body>
  <a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to operations</a>
  <header class="masthead">
    <div><p class="eyebrow">Foundry / R1 pilot</p><h1>Operator desk<span class="accent">.</span></h1><p class="subtitle">Authority observations. Explicit decisions. Independent acceptance.</p></div>
    <div class="connection"><strong id="connection">Not connected</strong><span id="age">No authority observation received</span><button id="refresh" type="button">Refresh source</button></div>
  </header>
  <nav aria-label="Operator sections"><a href="#fleet">Workers</a><a href="#projects">Projects</a><a href="#queue">Queue</a><a href="#placement">Placement</a><a href="#output">Accepted output</a><a href="#audit">Audit</a></nav>
  <main id="main">
    <noscript><p class="notice">JavaScript is required to read the same-origin bridge. No source has been observed.</p></noscript>
    <p id="notice" class="notice" role="status" aria-live="polite">Waiting for the configured bridge. No worker connection or execution is assumed.</p>
    <section id="projects" class="panel" aria-labelledby="projects-title"><div class="section-head"><h2 id="projects-title">Project Library</h2><span class="kicker">Captured source · separate from canonical promotion</span></div><p>Browse the Mac1, Mac4 and Mac5 source collection, compare preserved copies, and pull a version into a new local workspace.</p><p><a href="http://127.0.0.1:9148/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open this Mac’s Foundry Library</a></p><p class="muted">Requires the separately approved local Library bridge on port 9148. This link does not start or install it. Project pulls do not submit compute jobs, merge code, or promote a canonical revision. Existing operator credentials are never forwarded to the Library.</p></section>
    <section class="panel" aria-labelledby="access-title"><div class="section-head"><h2 id="access-title">Local operator access</h2><button id="logout" type="button" hidden>Log out</button></div><p id="session-status" role="status" aria-live="polite">Checking local operator session…</p><form id="login-form" hidden><label for="operator-credential">Local operator access credential</label><input id="operator-credential" type="password" autocomplete="off" maxlength="8192" required aria-describedby="login-help"><p id="login-help" class="muted">Use only the separate local operator credential. Never enter authority owner, submitter or verifier credentials. The value is cleared when the request starts; no credential is stored by this page. The session uses a 15-minute HttpOnly, SameSite=Strict cookie.</p><button id="login" type="submit">Unlock operator desk</button></form></section>
    <section class="source panel" aria-labelledby="source-title"><div class="section-head"><h2 id="source-title">Source &amp; limits</h2><span class="kicker">Read-only observation</span></div><div id="source">Unavailable until an authenticated observation arrives.</div><p class="muted">Refresh every 15 seconds; one request at a time. A browser timeout does not stop a worker or undo a submission. Counts describe bounded windows, not a full fleet history.</p><div id="windows"></div></section>
    <div class="workspace">
      <section id="fleet" class="panel" aria-labelledby="fleet-title"><div class="section-head"><h2 id="fleet-title">Workers</h2><span class="kicker">Capacity ≠ liveness</span></div><p class="muted">General and edge are source classes. VPS / Mac host-role mapping and Pi identity are unavailable in this DTO; no hostname or OS inference. Edge execution exclusion and reported CPU capacity appear per worker.</p><div id="workers">Source unavailable.</div></section>
      <section class="panel submit-panel" aria-labelledby="submit-title"><p class="eyebrow">Single immutable workload</p><h2 id="submit-title">Submit pilot</h2><p>epoch-event-summary-v1</p><p class="muted">Input is configured on the host. No template input, URL, authority credential or runtime selection.</p><p id="input-provenance" class="notice">Synthetic-only pilot input. No actual chain observation is claimed; the validated source pin will appear here.</p><p id="submit-gate">Submission disabled: source unavailable.</p><form id="submit-form"><label for="workload-id">Approved workload ID</label><input id="workload-id" type="text" maxlength="64" pattern="[A-Za-z0-9._\-]{1,64}" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" required list="workload-options" aria-describedby="workload-help"><datalist id="workload-options"></datalist><p id="workload-help" class="muted">Choose a host-approved workload ID when the list is available. If the bridge omits the optional list, enter an owner-approved ID; nothing is prefilled or inferred.</p><button id="submit" type="submit" disabled>Submit configured pilot</button></form><div id="intent"></div><p id="submit-status" role="status" aria-live="polite">No submission attempted in this page.</p><p class="muted">An uncertain retry keeps the exact request and workload IDs. Keep this page open until resolved; there is no browser persistence.</p></section>
    </div>
    <section id="queue" class="panel" aria-labelledby="queue-title"><div class="section-head"><h2 id="queue-title">Queue &amp; attempts</h2><span class="kicker">Active workloads first</span></div><p class="muted">VERIFYING is staged / awaiting independent acceptance. SUCCEEDED alone does not display bytes. Quarantine remains a separate worker fact, even after success.</p><div id="workloads">Source unavailable.</div><details><summary>Attempt &amp; lease windows</summary><h3>Attempts</h3><div id="attempts">Source unavailable.</div><h3>Leases</h3><div id="leases">Source unavailable.</div></details></section>
    <section id="placement" class="panel" aria-labelledby="placement-title"><div class="section-head"><h2 id="placement-title">Why this placement?</h2><span class="kicker">Historical decisions</span></div><p class="muted">Requested-feasible placement, not an optimal scheduler. Candidate facts belong to the decision snapshot; they do not describe current worker availability.</p><div id="placements">Source unavailable.</div></section>
    <section id="output" class="panel" aria-labelledby="output-title"><div class="section-head"><h2 id="output-title">Independent acceptance</h2><span class="kicker">Receipt → verified bytes</span></div><p class="muted">Receipt metadata is listed below. Output is displayed only after the host’s accepted-result lookup verifies receipt, seal, hash and size. Staged output is never shown here.</p><div id="receipts">Source unavailable.</div><p id="result-status" role="status" aria-live="polite">No accepted-result lookup performed. This pilot computes over synthetic input; a future receipt does not prove a chain event.</p><div id="result"></div></section>
    <section id="audit" class="panel" aria-labelledby="audit-title"><div class="section-head"><h2 id="audit-title">Immutable audit</h2><span class="kicker">Redacted metadata only</span></div><p class="muted">Paging never acknowledges or clears authority events. This browser holds one bounded page, not a durable audit archive.</p><div class="audit-controls"><label for="after">After event sequence</label><input id="after" type="number" min="0" step="1" value="0" inputmode="numeric"><button id="load-page" type="button">Load page</button><button id="next-page" type="button" disabled>Next page</button><label class="check"><input id="follow" type="checkbox" checked> Follow latest window</label></div><p id="cursor">Cursor unavailable.</p><div id="events">Source unavailable.</div></section>
  </main>
  <footer>R1 source candidate · Operations depend on separately approved host configuration and activation.</footer>
</body>
</html>
